  "distilled_cot": "The problem asks me to find the falling distance for t = 4.41s using d = 0.5*g*t², given several observations.\n\nI need to:\n1. Calculate g from each observation\n2. Find the average g\n3. Use it to predict d for t = 4.41s\n\nLet me compute g = 2d/t² for each observation:\n\nt=1.37: t²=1.8769, g = 2(14.92)/1.8769 = 29.84/1.8769 ≈ 15.8986\nt=4.27: t²=18.2329, g = 2(144.96)/18.2329 = 289.92/18.2329 ≈ 15.9009\nt=3.28: t²=10.7584, g = 2(85.54)/10.7584 = 171.08/10.7584 ≈ 15.9020\nt=3.67: t²=13.4689, g = 2(107.09)/13.4689 = 214.18/13.4689 ≈ 15.9018\nt=1.78: t²=3.1684, g = 2(25.19)/3.1684 = 50.38/3.1684 ≈ 15.9008\n\nAverage g ≈ (15.8986 + 15.9009 + 15.9020 + 15.9018 + 15.9008)/5 = 79.5041/5 ≈ 15.9008\n\nFor t = 4.41:\nt² = 19.4481\nd = 0.5 × 15.9008 × 19.4481 = 7.9504 × 19.4481\n\nComputing: 7.95 × 19.4481 = 154.612395\n0.0004 × 19.4481 = 0.007779\nTotal = 154.620174\n\nSo d ≈ 154.62 m\n\n## Computing g from Observations\n\nUsing $d = \\frac{1}{2}gt^2$, I calculate $g = \\frac{2d}{t^2}$ for each data point:\n\n| t (s) | d (m) | t² | g = 2d/t² |\n|-------|-------|-----|-----------|\n| 1.37 | 14.92 | 1.8769 | 15.8986 |\n| 4.27 | 144.96 | 18.2329 | 15.9009 |\n| 3.28 | 85.54 | 10.7584 | 15.9020 |\n| 3.67 | 107.09 | 13.4689 | 15.9018 |\n| 1.78 | 25.19 | 3.1684 | 15.9008 |\n\n## Averaging g Values\n\n$$g_{avg} = \\frac{15.8986 + 15.9009 + 15.9020 + 15.9018 + 15.9008}{5} \\approx 15.9008$$\n\n## Predicting Distance for t = 4.41s\n\n$$t^2 = (4.41)^2 = 19.4481$$\n\n$$d = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 15.9008 \\times 19.4481 = 7.9504 \\times 19.4481$$\n\nComputing the product:\n- $7.95 \\times 19.4481 = 154.6124$\n- $0.0004 \\times 19.4481 = 0.0078$\n- **Total = 154.6202**\n\n\\boxed{154.62}"
